  "description": "E37 arm e37a_c32 — concept memory, 32 keys per concept, 30M testbed. New against e37a_s30: compression ladder: 16 concepts of 32 keys per block (same 512 opened tokens; only the summaries get coarser). Protocol: 1.5B FineWeb-Edu tokens in rows of 4,096, then a 0.2B LongDocs-lite decay in rows of 16,384, 64 rows per step (E33p stage 1). Built 2026-11-07; status training (as of 2026-11-08). Training on Polonez GPUs 0+1; main phase due about 13:10 UTC 8 Nov; its evals were not written yet at arch-10m 7c7158c (13:40 UTC). Spec: docs/experiments_specs/ahead/E37_concept_memory.md. Source: origin/arch-10m @ 6e49738. Not a builder field: Grouping, statistics and the choice have no weights (0-parameter custom cells); the summaries are the concepts' mean key and value (a notes cell with no projections); the block window and opened tokens are drawn as a 1,280-key window. The summaries' length scale (concept_sum_len: past that length their total weight is held at its level) has no weights and no builder field. The 30M runs trained without it and use it as an eval switch (arch-10m e9b37d2); from stage A the concept arms train with it set to the decay's row length, 16,384, where it is inert (arch-10m 7c7158c, 8 Nov). Parameters: 68,701,396 in total, 26,260,308 without the word tables (input embedding 13,493,056 + output layer 28,948,032); exact against the trainer's own count (evaluation/text_checks.count_params on scripts/run_e33n.py --arm e37a_c32 --size s30 (FFN 1472 from fit())). The testbed is called “30M” after the notebook arms' 30.2M without word tables (Kaplan et al.'s convention).",
